{{ElectionsOR}}
The '''2018 United States House of Representatives elections in Oregon''' will be held on Tuesday, November 6, 2018, to elect the five [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representatives]] from the [[U.S. state]] of [[Oregon]]; one from each of the state's five congressional districts. Primaries were held on May 15, 2018. The elections and primaries will coincide with the elections and primaries of other federal and state offices.
{{Toclimit|limit=2}}

==District 1==
{{seealso|Oregon's 1st congressional district}}
The 1st district is located in [[Northwest Oregon|northwestern Oregon]] and streches from [[Oregon Coast #North Coast|coastal cities]] of the [[Astoria, OR|Astoria]] and [[Seaside, OR|Seaside]], to the [[Northwest District, Portland, Oregon| parts of Portland]] and the surrounding suburbs such as [[Beaverton, OR|Beaverton]], [[Hillsboro, OR|Hillsboro]], and [[Newberg, OR|Newberg]]. This district has a PVI of D+9. The incumbent is Democrat [[Suzanne Bonamici]], who has represented the district since 2012. She was re-elected with 60% of the vote in 2016. She will face Republican nominee John Verbeek in the November 2018 general election.

